Z||000000||Ludo||05-01-2001||09:22 AM||||I have bought a fiero SE 2.5 86, but there are problems with the gauges, there's nothing that work. only the oilpresure is working. Its very difficult to find some information over this car here in Belgium.<BR>I must need a technical book or something about the elektronic circuits. Is there anybody who can help me?||||reg||5
Z||000001||84Bill||05-01-2001||12:31 PM||||K there are several plugs that run the electronics under the dash. You will need to remove the 5 screws securing the upper cover and the 4 on the lower panel. There is a plug on the L/H side bottom of the cluster this is the Speedo connector. The one on the left rear is the gages and lights and the right rear is the Tach and lights. make sure they are attached properly. some folks when they remove the plugs bend the copper contacts out so you might want check that. There is also 2 connectors under the rear console. They cross over from the internal harness to the engine harness. The connector is just under the ECM usually clear or white and it will run from the (looking at ecm) left harness to the right. be sure one of them has not become disconnected.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||05-01-2001||02:33 PM||||Try this link for help:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html</A> <P>Also check Ogre's Cave link at the bottom of this page.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
